Subtask 5.5: Create a Simple Test Integration
Create a simple Camel route to test the integration.

# Create a test directory
mkdir -p ~/fuse-test

# Create a simple Camel route XML file
cat > ~/fuse-test/simple-route.xml << 'EOF'
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<blueprint xmlns="http://www.osgi.org/xmlns/blueprint/v1.0.0"
           xmlns:camel="http://camel.apache.org/schema/blueprint">

  <camelContext xmlns="http://camel.apache.org/schema/blueprint">
    <route id="simple-file-route">
      <from uri="file:///tmp/camel-input?noop=true"/>
      <log message="Processing file: ${header.CamelFileName}"/>
      <to uri="file:///tmp/camel-output"/>
    </route>
  </camelContext>

</blueprint>
EOF

# Create test directories
mkdir -p /tmp/camel-input /tmp/camel-output

# Create a test file
echo "Hello from Red Hat Fuse!" > /tmp/camel-input/test-message.txt
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Java Version Conflicts
If you encounter Java version issues:

# Check current Java version
java -version

# List available Java versions
sudo alternatives --config java

# Set the correct Java version
sudo alternatives --set java /usr/lib/jvm/java-11-openjdk/bin/java
Issue 2: Port Conflicts
If services fail to start due to port conflicts:

# Check what's using the ports
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep :61616  # ActiveMQ
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep :8161   # ActiveMQ Web Console
sudo netstat -tlnp | grep :8101   # Karaf SSH

# Kill conflicting processes if necessary
sudo fuser -k 61616/tcp
Issue 3: Permission Issues
If you encounter permission errors:

# Fix ownership of installation directories
sudo chown -R $USER:$USER /opt/apache-camel
sudo chown -R $USER:$USER /opt/apache-karaf
sudo chown -R $USER:$USER /opt/apache-activemq

# Ensure execute permissions on scripts
chmod +x $KARAF_HOME/bin/*
chmod +x $ACTIVEMQ_HOME/bin/*
